  "upload": {
    "title": "KFC's Secret Recipe Is Locked in Concrete 🍗 #shorts",
    "description": "KFC says Colonel Sanders' handwritten 1940 Original Recipe of 11 herbs and spices is kept in a digital safe encased in two feet of concrete and monitored around the clock by video and motion detection. The company also uses separate suppliers for the blend so no single supplier knows the whole recipe. The twist: in 2016 the Colonel's nephew, Joe Ledington, showed a Chicago Tribune reporter a family scrapbook with a handwritten list of 11 herbs and spices. The Tribune's test kitchen found its fried chicken only became virtually indistinguishable from KFC after adding MSG. KFC says the list is not the real recipe.",
